meta {
  name: Container recommendation history (with expl columns)
  type: http
  seq: 15
}

get {
  url: {{baseURL}}/recommendations/openshift/history?cluster={{clusterAlias}}&container=grafana&filter[engine]=cost&term=short_term&limit=5
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  cluster: {{clusterAlias}}
  container: grafana
  filter[engine]: cost
  term: short_term
  limit: 5
}

docs {
  Container recommendation history with explanation columns exposed.

  The response now includes 21 expl_* columns providing context for each
  recommendation snapshot:
  - expl_data_days, expl_decay_half_life_hours
  - expl_cpu_cost_pct_mc, expl_cpu_perf_pct_mc, expl_cpu_usage_p95_mc,
    expl_cpu_usage_p50_mc, expl_cpu_usage_mean_mc, expl_cpu_adaptive_margin_bp,
    expl_cpu_trend_slope
  - expl_mem_cost_pct_kib, expl_mem_perf_pct_kib, expl_mem_usage_p95_kib,
    expl_mem_usage_p50_kib, expl_mem_usage_mean_kib, expl_mem_adaptive_margin_bp,
    expl_mem_trend_slope
  - expl_oom_count_sum, expl_oom_bump_applied, expl_cpu_floor_applied,
    expl_mem_floor_applied, expl_is_idle

  Term filter accepts canonical forms: short_term, medium_term, long_term.
  Legacy values (short, medium, long) are also normalized automatically.
  Response always returns the canonical form.

  Used by the frontend Container Recommendation History Chart (issue #49).

  `cluster` (and filter[cluster]) matches the cluster alias, exact match —
  pass the cluster_alias value from the row/detail response, NOT the cluster
  UUID (a UUID returns 0 rows unless it happens to be the alias). #696.
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}
